    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="1078" n="942" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg942"/>

                <head>No. 674.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-15"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 15, 1888</date>.
                        (Received November 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 220.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Boston</hi> intends leaving here to-morrow morning direct for New York and
                    will communicate immediately with the Navy Department and send full details as
                    to the case of the steam-ship <hi rendition="#italic">Haytian Republic</hi> and
                    that of the schooner <hi rendition="#italic">William Jones.</hi></p>
                <p>I will forward my report to the Department on these two cases as soon as it can
                    be prepared, as the questions contain a great deal of reading matter.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John E. W.
                    Thompson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
